<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to offer 2yr bonds of HUF 5bln on March 17.</title>
<headline>Hungary to offer 2yr bonds of HUF 5bln on March 17.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will issue 5 billion forint worth of the two-year government bonds of 1999/F series between March 17 and 21, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period     3 March 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    12 April 1999</p>
<p>    Bills on offer			5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price		   To be published on March 14</p>
<p>Average price of two-year</p>
<p>bonds at last auction (Feb 27) 97.66 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.5 percent, payable semi- anually starting from October 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
